  "schema": "transfer-verification-equality-endpoint-v1",
  "scope": "Functional Verification::eq and Verified::ensure_binds compare the actual family, statement scalar and serialized envelope bytes. Success derives every compared field and requested family. Registry identifier independence is explicit. Mismatched fields refuse symbolically; no runtime negative-control credit. Exact fieldwise item matching dispatches the qualified capability wrapper. Crypto verification, statement-preimage/semantic correspondence, actual scalar/serializer codecs, native execution, atomic evidence refresh and full Transfer remain open. The public instance generated by deriving DecidableEq is explicitly audited. Operational conjunction equality is equivalent to equality of the three represented fields; this instantiates generic item comparison in the capability wrapper. ensure_binds success recovers requested family and all compared fields; registry independence is explicitly proved because that method does not inspect registry_id. Scalar/envelope equality does not establish proof validity, source statement preimage equality, cryptographic hash injectivity, registry provenance or semantic correspondence. Field-mismatch refusals are logical model conclusions only.",
